<!--
    WayDrop status-bar notification icon.

    Android renders notification small icons as a flat monochrome (alpha-only) silhouette;
    the OS ignores color entirely and re-tints every pixel, and it must read clearly at a fixed
    ~24dp. The full WayDrop marketing logo (assets/images/waydrop_logo_transparent.png) is thin
    multi-element line art (car outline + sunburst + rider + parcel) that was test-rendered at
    24/36/48px and came out as an illegible faint blur at any of those sizes; there is no
    resampling that fixes that, the source art itself is too fine-detailed for this slot. This is
    a simplified, bold, solid silhouette of the car, the dominant shape in the actual logo,
    which is what's actually legible in a status bar. A vector drawable is used (not a rasterized
    PNG set) so it stays crisp at every density without needing five separate exported bitmaps.
-->
